# Windsurf Rules for LeechBot

## Project
Pyrogram 2.0.106 Telegram bot for file transloading. Python 3.10+, asyncio, ~8000 lines.

## Quick Reference
- Entry: `leechbot/__main__.py`
- Commands: `leechbot/commands.py`
- State: `leechbot/utility/variables.py`
- Config: `config.py`
- Downloaders: `leechbot/downloader/*.py`
- Uploaders: `leechbot/uploader/telegram.py`
- Dashboard: `leechbot/web/server.py` + `public/index.html`
- Agent docs: `AGENTS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`

## Patterns
- All state in class attributes — import and mutate directly
- `from leechbot import app` for Pyrogram client
- Async handlers with `@app.on_message()` / `@app.on_callback_query()`
- `logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)` at module top
- Standard file header block on every `.py` file

## Constraints
- No `progress` on `reply_media_group()` — upload individually then group via `file_id`
- No `style` on `InlineKeyboardButton` — Pyrogram 2.0.106 predates it
- Telegram 2GB file limit, media group max 10 photos
- No test suite, no CI/CD

## Changelog
New entry at top of `CHANGELOG.md` for every change. Never edit existing entries.
